@using JobPortal.Web.Models;

@model List<LibraryModel>
@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Library";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";

}
@Html.Partial("_Breadcrumb")
@section HeaderImage
{
    <div class="headerImage2">
        <img src="~/images/jobs-new.png" />
    </div>
}
<div class="academicregprofiletopbg">
</div>
<div class="hometext academicregprofile" style="margin-top:2px">
    <ul class="ulBreadcrumb" style="padding-top:10px;">
        <li><a href="/">Home <span class="fa fa-angle-right"></span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/home/academicreg">Academics</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="commonPara paraHeader" style="text-align:center">
        <b>Which Door Can Rewrite the Institution’s DNA? </b>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara " style="text-align:center; margin:0px auto"> <img src="~/images/academic.png" /></p>
    <p class="commonPara paraHeader" style="text-align:center; margin:0px auto">
        No rankings. No judgment. Just clarity.
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara" style="padding-top:20px">
        <b>Door 1: The Academic Institution Identity</b>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara">
        First, let there be an <i>Academic Profile</i>, not a brochure, but a living snapshot of your teaching depth, research instincts, industry exposure, and future intent. It is Important your profile reflects “Not who you are on paper - but what you actually stand for as a teacher, researcher, and thinker”.
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara"></p>
     

      <p class="commonPara">
        <b>Door 2: The Practice</b>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara">
        Second, <i>the academic and institutional prowess</i> talk about you - what you teach well, what you experiment with, where you’re ahead of the curve in green domains. Where your classrooms, labs, and ideas quietly outperform others especially in green domains.
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara"></p>

    <p class="commonPara">
        <b>Door 3: The Talent Magnet</b>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara">
        Third, <i>better students</i> are attracted where talent sees clarity, not brochures. Why the right internships and placement gravitate toward clarity, not glossy prospectuses.
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara"></p>

    <p class="commonPara">
        <b>Door 4: The Mirror</b>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara">
        Fourth, <i>rankings and benchmark</i>, where your institution stands on a Green Education & Employability Matrix, not to compete blindly, but to improve intelligently. A benchmark that shows gaps, strengths, and blind spots - without league-table anxiety.
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara"></p>

    <p class="commonPara">
        <b>Door 5: The Employer Connect</b>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara">
        Finally, <i>plugging into employers</i> - co-creating curricula, training modules, internships, and live problem statements that actually matter. Where education meets real-world problems, live curricula, and meaningful collaboration.
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara"></p>


    <p class="commonPara">
        <b>Join hands with us.</b>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara">
        Work with us to translate clarity into outcomes - admissions, internships, employer trust, and compliance.
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara"></p>
    <p class="commonPara">

        <span> <a href="/visitor/openSurvey/8" class="homeImage"><img src="~/images/profile.png" width="70px" /></a></span>
    </p>
    <p class="commonPara"></p>
</div>